  "modified": "2026-09-07T12:45:51Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Heap buffer overflow in to_char(timestamptz).\n     DCH_to_char() copies the timezone abbreviation into a\n     DCH_MAX_ITEM_SIZ-budgeted workspace with an unchecked strcpy(), and\n     any client can select a longer POSIX abbreviation via SET TIME ZONE\n     (CVSS 8.8, arbitrary code execution as the database OS user).\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14669.patch: reject POSIX timezone\n       abbreviations longer than n->key->len * DCH_MAX_ITEM_SIZ in the\n       TZ/tz items of DCH_to_char() with an error, instead of strcpy()ing\n       them past the palloc'd buffer (upstream 3d724bf4fd by Tom Lane,\n       carried on REL_14_STABLE inside 5fb3c63 and shipped in 14.24;\n       applies verbatim to 12.22).\n     - CVE-2026-14669",
